From: Tom Plant <tom@tplant.com.au>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3568: imply EFI_LOADER_BOUNCE_BUFFER

The RK3566/RK3568 SD/MMC controllers (dw_mmc) only support 32-bit
IDMAC addresses. On boards with more than 4 GiB of RAM, U-Boot adds
the DRAM above 4 GiB as a second bank and the EFI loader allocates
buffers there. EFI block I/O then programs the DMA with a truncated
address, so reads land in the wrong place and the boot hangs at
random, either in the boot manager while reading the ESP or in GRUB
while loading the kernel.

Seen on an 8 GiB Pine64 SOQuartz booting from microSD: efi_mgr hung
in 2 of 3 boots and GRUB hung loading the kernel, while "load" to
addresses below 4 GiB always worked.

Imply EFI_LOADER_BOUNCE_BUFFER so that EFI disk I/O goes through a
bounce buffer below 4 GiB.

---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig
@@ -383,6 +383,7 @@ config ROCKCHIP_RK3568
 	select DM_RESET
 	imply BOOTSTD_FULL
 	imply DM_RNG
+	imply EFI_LOADER_BOUNCE_BUFFER if EFI_LOADER
 	imply MISC_INIT_R
 	imply MMC_HS200_SUPPORT if MMC_SDHCI_ROCKCHIP
 	imply OF_LIBFDT_OVERLAY
-- 
